    <sys:String x:Key="Log_Title">What is blocked, and why</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_TabConflicts">URL conflicts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_HintConflicts">Where two tiles claim the same address or program. Any tile’s sites and templates outrank programs; between two tiles with the same address, the one further left wins.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_TipConflicts">Live log. Tiles conflict over addresses: {0} — see the “URL conflicts” tab.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfHarmlessRoute">No difference right now: “{0}” and “{1}” take the same route. It matters once you change the VPN, card or kill-switch of one of them.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfHarmlessPartial">Usually intended: a narrower address in “{0}” takes its part from a wider one in “{1}”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfNone">No conflicts: no address or program appears in two tiles.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWins">Works:</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWho">it stands left of “{1}”, so these addresses won’t work in “{1}”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWhoProg">it stands left of “{1}”: the program follows it, not “{1}”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWhoSilent">“{1}” has no VPN and no kill-switch, so it writes no rules — its addresses follow “{0}”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfSame">{0} — in both tiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfCovered">{0} from “{1}” is already covered by {2} from “{3}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfPartial">{0} from “{1}” takes part of {2} away from “{3}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfKeyword">the word “{0}” from “{1}” will catch {2} from “{3}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfIp">{0} from “{1}” lies inside {2} from “{3}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfProgram">{0} — in both tiles</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfMore">…and {0} more</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWhenOff">While “{0}” is off (its kill-switch is off), these addresses follow “{1}”.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfFix">For the right-hand tile to work: remove the address from the left one, or reorder the tiles.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfFixProg">Keep the program in one tile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfFolderPartial">{0} from “{1}” lies in the folder {2} from “{3}” and follows “{1}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfWhoFolder">it is more specific: a detected program file, a program or a nested folder beats the wider entry of “{1}”, whatever the order of the tiles.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfHarmlessFolder">Intended: the more specific entry in “{0}” (a detected file, a program or a nested folder) beats the wider one in “{1}” and takes its part.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_ConfFilePartial">this very file {0} (detected automatically) follows “{1}”; every other copy of {2} follows “{3}”</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_WhyAllBlock">Blocked by the “{0}” tile: “Block” is selected and the address belongs to no tile.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Log_WhyAllKill">Kill-switch of the “{0}” tile: its VPN is not up and the address belongs to no tile.</sys:String>
